      "name": "tables",
      "spec": ["decoding.md §7.1", "decoding.md §7.3", "decoding.md §7.5"],
      "note": "The points are (0, 0), (10, 100), (20, 150). t_lin 15 is in segment 1: 100 + ((15 - 10) x (150 - 100)) / (20 - 10) = 125. t_at 10 is a point's raw, so exactly its value, 100. Step interpolation gives the last point below 15, 100, and extrapolated past the end, the nearest end point's value, 150. Linear extrapolation continues the last segment: 100 + ((25 - 10) x 50) / 10 = 175. t_out 25 is outside without extrapolate, so it has no engineering value: out_of_calibration, with the raw 25.",
      "family": "conv",
      "message": { "hex": "04 0f 0a 0f 19 19 19", "metadata": {}, "ground_time": "2026-06-01T12:00:00Z" },
      "decoded": {
        "family": "conv",
        "native_id": "conv-1",
        "asset": "conv-1",
        "stand_in": true,
        "set": "conv_v1",
