      "name": "a-natural-cubic-spline",
      "spec": ["decoding.md §7.1"],
      "note": "The points are (0, 0), (10, 10), (25, 5), (30, 20): h = 10, 15, 5 and s = 1, -1/3, 3. The sweep gives c1 = 0.3, d1 = -0.16, c2 = 0.14084507042253522, d2 = 0.6309859154929577, so M2 = 0.6309859154929577 and M1 = d1 - c1 x M2 = -0.3492957746478873. s_in 21 is in segment 1, L = 4 and R = 11: the segment formula, evaluated in binary64 in the order written, M1 x L x L x L as ((M1 x L) x L) x L, gives 1.5573708920187794; grouping the cube first, M1 x (L x L x L), would give 1.5573708920187777. s_at 25 is a point's raw: 5. With extrapolate, s_hi 40 continues at the end slope, 20 + 10 x (3 + 5 x M2 / 6) = 55.25821596244131, and s_lo -5 below the start, 0 + -5 x (1 - 10 x M1 / 6) = -7.910798122065728.",
      "family": "conv",
      "message": { "hex": "05 15 19 28 fb", "metadata": {}, "ground_time": "2026-06-01T12:00:00Z" },
