    {
      "name": "sentinels-and-which-quality-wins",
      "spec": ["decoding.md §7.1", "decoding.md §7.2", "decoding.md §7.3", "decoding.md §7.5"],
      "note": "q_int 255 is its sentinel: invalid, with the raw value, for its sample too. q_str 9999 equals its string sentinel exactly. q_float -1.0 equals the integer sentinel -1 numerically. q_both 10 is its sentinel and its conversion gives 1e309, infinity, so both invalid and non_finite apply; the quality is the first that applies from the bottom of the order up, invalid, with the raw 10. q_inf reads infinity, which is outside the table's points, so both non_finite and out_of_calibration apply; from the bottom up non_finite comes first, with the raw value. flag 2 maps to a bool param: an integer that isn't 0 is true; its engineering value is the raw 2.",
      "family": "conv",
