    {
      "name": "a-fields-unit-into-its-params",
      "spec": ["decoding.md §7.3", "decoding.md §7.5", "units.md §2", "units.md §4"],
      "note": "mV's factor is 1e-3 x 1000 = 1 and V's 1000, so 1500 mV is (1500 x 1) / 1000 = 1.5 V. 25 Cel is 25 + 273.15 = 298.15 K, divided by K's factor 1. 0 [degF] is ((0 + 459.67) x 5) / 9 = 255.3722222222222 K, less 273.15: -17.77777777777777 Cel; multiplying by the reciprocal 5 / 9, which decoding.md forbids, would give -17.777777777777743. Each sample carries its param's unit; each engineering value stays in its field's unit, the raw integer.",
      "family": "conv",
      "message": { "hex": "07 05 dc 00 19 00 00", "metadata": {}, "ground_time": "2026-06-01T12:00:00Z" },
      "decoded": {
        "family": "conv",
